From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EvilMetaMonkey <hood.mj85@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:15:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add dmc checkpoint export <id> --to <dir> [--state
 before|after]

Writes the files of one checkpoint manifest (after by default; before
uses the begin manifest) to a new or empty directory outside the
workspace, for bisect. Bytes come from the snapshot store with every
SHA-256 verified, and modes are restored (one chmod per mode). Absent
entries, and left_scope/entered_scope files without a state in that
manifest, are not written.

Safety: the target must not exist or be an empty directory, must not be
or contain the workspace (checked on both the given and the
link-resolved paths), and is never followed if it is a link. Files are
written to a temporary sibling and renamed into place, so a failed
export (for example, a corrupted snapshot) leaves nothing behind. The
workspace operation lock is held only while the manifest is read.

--json --schema-version 1 returns checkpointId, state, directory,
fileCount, totalBytes and manifestSha256. capabilities lists
checkpoint.export and the features checkpointExport and
policyDriftPerFile.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
